<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/talks-ted-processing> {
  ex:ted-data-processing a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "From raw data to polymer content"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:ted-processing-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-processing-description ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-processing-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "The described TED-GC-MS workflow imports Shimadzu GQD files, detects and describes chromatographic peaks in each extracted-ion chromatogram (EIC) with qPeaks, jointly fits features with a shared elution profile into components, selects polymer marker components and applies external calibration. GQD is the file designation supplied by the method author; import compatibility is not independently verified here."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-processing-description ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-qpeaks a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "qPeaks peak detection"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:ted-qpeaks-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-processing-description ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-qpeaks-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "qPeaks scans every EIC with a moving regression window, repeating the scan at several window sizes to find and describe peaks. In the author's description, the response is log-transformed and modeled by an asymmetric piecewise quadratic: ylog = b0 + b1*x + b2*x^2 for x < 0, and ylog = b0 + b1*x + b3*x^2 otherwise. Here ylog is log response, x is the local time coordinate relative to the branch origin, b0 is the intercept, b1 the shared linear coefficient, and b2 and b3 the left and right curvature coefficients; * denotes multiplication and ^2 squaring. The precise log base, coordinate scaling and fit acceptance rules are not specified in this overview. Inverse normal matrices (X transpose X) inverse are precomputed for the applicable design matrices, avoiding repeated matrix inversion. The author reports peak/component lists in seconds; this is not an independently reproduced benchmark or a universal runtime guarantee."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-processing-description ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-peak-components a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Jointly fitted chromatographic components"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:ted-components-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-processing-description ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-components-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "A feature is a chromatographic peak in an individual EIC. A component groups features sharing an elution profile and estimated jointly with one extended parallel peak model. The shape coefficients are shared across channels; channel-specific intercepts in log space allow individual heights after back-transformation. Thus b0 becomes a vector with one intercept per EIC while the linear and left/right quadratic shape terms remain shared. This computational grouping is not by itself proof of a unique chemical identity. Component formation is followed by marker selection and external calibration."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-processing-description ; cd:authoredResource true .
}
<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/sources/talks-ted-processing> {
  ex:ted-source-processing-description a cd:Source ; dct:title "TED data-processing workflow: method author's presentation specification" ; dct:creator "Gerrit Renner" ; dct:identifier "issue-294/processing-overview-author-description" ; dct:description "Author-supplied workflow and qPeaks model description. No independent software benchmark, importer test or chemical-identification validation is claimed."@en ; cd:supportsResource ex:ted-processing-definition, ex:ted-qpeaks-definition, ex:ted-components-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
}
